  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for sssd",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for sssd fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-68742: insufficient validation in the NSS responder can lead to an out-of-bounds read and a process crash\n  when a crafted GETHOSTBYADDR request is sent to the NSS responder socket (bsc#1273922).\n- CVE-2026-68743: insufficient validation in the PAM responder can lead to an out-of-bounds read and a process crash\n  when a crafted protocol v1 request is processed (bsc#1273925).\n- CVE-2026-68744: improper memory management in the NSS responder can lead to uninitialized heap memory disclosure\n  from the `sssd_nss` process (bsc#1273924).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
